#: includes/class-sspa-tools.php:501
#, php-format
msgid ""
"Hello,\n"
"\n"
"I am diagnosing a performance problem on my WordPress site and need read access to MySQL's performance_schema statistics.\n"
"\n"
"Could you please:\n"
"1. Ensure performance_schema is enabled on the database server (MariaDB has it off by default).\n"
"2. Run: %1$s\n"
"\n"
"This is read-only access to query statistics. It grants no access to any data and cannot modify anything.\n"
"\n"
"MySQL version reported to my site: %2$s\n"
"\n"
"Thank you."
msgstr ""

#. translators: 1: PHP extension name, 2: PHP version, 3: PHP interface, 4: operating system, 5: PHP configuration directory, 6: installation commands
#: includes/class-sspa-tools.php:527
#, php-format
msgid ""
"Hello,\n"
"\n"
"I am diagnosing a performance problem on my WordPress site and would like the PHP extension \"%1$s\" installed.\n"
"\n"
"It is free and open source, it runs entirely on the server, and it sends no data anywhere. It is a diagnostic profiler.\n"
"\n"
"My environment as far as I can see it:\n"
"- PHP %2$s (%3$s)\n"
"- %4$s\n"
"- PHP ini scan directory: %5$s\n"
"\n"
"The usual install is:\n"
